  "slug": "space-minimizers-77f8",
  "summary": "Recent preprints report concrete memory, compression, and query-speed gains for k-mer indexes over pan-genome and TCR data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is explicit space-time trade-off engineering in k-mer data structures. Super Bloom groups filter entries by minimizer to enable faster, cache-efficient streaming queries with fewer false positives via findere. Pareto optimization of masked superstrings jointly trades superstring length against mask runs, reporting 12-19% better compression of pan-genome k-mer sets. TCRseek applies windowed k-mer embeddings with FAISS indexes and alignment reranking to approximate nearest-neighbor search over TCR CDR3 repertoires, reporting 3.6-39.6x speedups over its comparison. What is new in this set is the explicit Pareto formulation of superstring compression and the minimizer-grouped filter layout for cache-friendly lookup. All three items are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-03-25"
}
